      "description": "Ascenty's São Paulo Capital Campus is a significant data center infrastructure located in Osasco, Brazil, designed to support digital transformation and hybrid IT scalability. The campus comprises six distinct data centers, each offering state-of-the-art facilities and robust security measures.\n\nSão Paulo 1 provides 6 MW of power across 3,500 sqm, with strategic access to major highways and airports. São Paulo 2, situated in Brazil's largest financial center, offers 14 MW over 8,000 sqm with advanced technology and energy efficiency. São Paulo 3, near telecommunications hubs, delivers 4 MW on 4,000 sqm for maximum performance. São Paulo 4, integrated into a technology ecosystem, provides 9 MW across 7,500 sqm for comprehensive data storage and processing solutions. São Paulo 5, in the city's industrial center, features 6 MW on 7,000 sqm for efficiency and resilience. Finally, São Paulo 6, in a high-density business area, offers 8 MW over 7,000 sqm with continuous technical support and advanced security.\n\nAll data centers within the campus are carrier-neutral, ensuring high levels of connectivity for businesses operating within this strategic location.",
